A||||5||jlruiz67||what happens when you drive with a big exhaust leak?||||1||
Z||000000||jlruiz67||01-28-2001||01:12 PM||||Can anyone tell me the real risk of running my Fiero with a huge leak on my exhaust manifold for a couple of weeks, I don't want to mess anything else up but I do need to use a car to go to work and back and I'm short on cash for a rental.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/005467.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/005467.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Shiner||01-28-2001||01:52 PM||||The engine bay temps will be off the charts.  You could possibly melt wiring harnesses.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||01-28-2001||02:45 PM||||An exhaust leak creates all sorts of problems.<P>Like shinner said plus if it's a big leak you have potential for fire and CO poisoning. The eninge bay is not entirely air tight from the passenger compartment. CO can build up in the cabin allot faster than you might think.<P>Even a small leak screws up performance and emmissions. It lets exhaust out but it also lets air in, screwing up the O2 sensor output.||||reg||1
Z||000003||bHooper||01-28-2001||02:49 PM||||you can easily tell, with the sunroof open, that the cabin sucks air in from the rear deck.<P>at least on my GT, i can.<P>but i am trying to fix the big leak.<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||01-28-2001||04:57 PM||||not to mention burned valves||||reg||1
Z||000005||JasonC||01-29-2001||09:04 AM||||I used to have an old 78 Toyota pickup truck with a 20R engine. It had a crack in the exhaust manifold and would occasionally throw a manifold bolt, one would just loosen up and fall out. Once it loosened up and actually shot out, ya know from excessive accelleration…<P>It had something like 240,000 miles when I finally sold it, crack and all. I got it with 130,000, and it had the crack then also.<P>Engine was/is one heck of a motor, but it's also a Toyota, and there pretty much was no such thing as any kind of sensors in there.<P>Just a little bit of info to ponder.<P>------------------<BR>Jason Carmichael<BR> <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net2/smile-r.gif"> <A HREF="http://www.getpaid2surf.net/97GPGT" TARGET=_blank>My GP GT on the net.</A> <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net2/smile-l.gif"> ||||reg||6
